From c9b9a1f45183bde067636d0c243bafe8468fec23 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John <john.de.kroon@cyberant.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 14:45:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 02/13] client: BADGE=1 step B, leave out the HF protocols the
 badge does not need

Without aliro, cipurse, cryptorf, epa, emrtd, felica, fido, fmcos, secc,
fudan, gallagher, gst, ict, jooki, ksx6924, lto, ntag424, saflok, tesla,
texkom, vas and xerox (also in hf search), the 530 KB smart card ATR table,
the overlay graph buffer (Qt only) and the flasher animation. Also the
LOWMEM fallback for even32() that crapto1.c lacked.

Measured (riscv32 bFLT): text 1.73 MB, data 1.04 MB, bss 1.39 MB, 4.26 MB
in all, from 40 MB for the full client.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
